---
import { RESUME_URL } from '../data/links';
---

<section id="experience">
  <h2 class="sec-h">Experience</h2>
  <ol class="jobs">
    {/* data-file names each entry in the shell's ~/experience */}
    <li class="job" data-file="metech.txt">
      <p class="job-when">2026</p>
      <div>
        <h3>COO and Technical Lead <span>· ME Tech</span></h3>
        <p class="job-desc">
          Five-person software contracting company in Japan. Set coding standards, code review and security
          requirements, managed two engineers, onboarded three, and ran planning with the CEO.
        </p>
        <ul class="job-wins">
          <li>Solo Rails 4.2 to Rails 7.1 upgrade of a school platform used by two schools and about 800 students, backed by 8,000+ unit tests built with Claude Code and reviewed one by one</li>
          <li>A second Rails backend upgraded, with 500+ new tests</li>
          <li>About 40% faster photo loading and about 15% faster pages</li>
          <li>School onboarding 25% shorter; accidental organization sign-ups cut from about 3 a month to zero</li>
          <li>GitHub Actions CI/CD and Capistrano deploys to AWS EC2 and S3</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="job-tech">Ruby on Rails, Vue.js, TypeScript, Python, PostgreSQL, AWS, Stripe, Claude Code</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="job" data-file="teaching.txt">
      <p class="job-when">2024 – now</p>
      <div>
        <h3>English Teacher <span>· Osaka</span></h3>
        <p class="job-desc">
          One-on-one and group lessons for students aged 1 to 65 at Dorothy EQ Plaza, Little Stars English and
          Mac's English School (as a substitute), plus private students. Custom lesson plans, including
          CLIL-based lessons and business English.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="job" data-file="independent.txt">
      <p class="job-when">2022 – 2025</p>
      <div>
        <h3>Independent Developer <span>· Remote</span></h3>
        <p class="job-desc">
          Remote work while traveling: development, QA and project management on Echoes of Undeath, a two-person
          Unity game now in Early Access on Steam. Also the Dorothy EQ Plaza website, and planning help for small teams.
        </p>
        <p class="job-tech">Unity, C#, HTML, CSS, JavaScript</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="job" data-file="vocera.txt">
      <p class="job-when">2014 – 2021</p>
      <div>
        <h3>Platform Developer II and Scrum Master <span>· Vocera Communications</span></h3>
        <p class="job-prev">
          Previously Platform Developer I (2016 – 2018) and Junior Platform Developer, part-time (2014 – 2016), Extension Healthcare
        </p>
        <p class="job-desc">
          Backend for a platform that routes alerts, calls and messages to hospital staff. Rails and PostgreSQL
          APIs, device integration over XMPP and Java, and the RHEL servers underneath. Ran scrum for an
          international team, led customer escalations and mentored new hires.
        </p>
        <ul class="job-wins">
          <li>A hot PostgreSQL query rewritten to run 70% faster, speeding up logins and chat at shift change</li>
          <li>Dual-node failover with keepalived</li>
          <li>Reliable message delivery on OpenMQ inside Glassfish</li>
          <li>Throttled background processing for heavy jobs</li>
          <li>The onboarding plan for interns and new hires</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="job-tech">Ruby on Rails, PostgreSQL, Java, XMPP, RHEL, Apache, Glassfish, AngularJS</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="job" data-file="its.txt">
      <p class="job-when">2013 – 2014</p>
      <div>
        <h3>Web Application Developer, part-time student worker <span>· IT Services, IPFW</span></h3>
        <p class="job-desc">Built web pages and database tables in Groovy and Grails, working directly with the people who asked for them.</p>
        <p class="job-tech">Groovy, Grails</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="creds" data-file="education.txt">
    B.S. Computer Science, Purdue University Fort Wayne (then IPFW), 2017. JLPT N5, 2024. Certified ScrumMaster and
    Certified SAFe 5 Practitioner, both earned in 2021 and no longer active.
    <a href={RESUME_URL} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full résumé <svg class="ico" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow" /></svg></a>
  </p>
</section>
